<title>USA: South Dakota unemployment down 0.1 pct in April.</title>
<headline>South Dakota unemployment down 0.1 pct in April.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Dakota's unemployment rate dropped 0.1 percent in April to 2.7 percent, 0.6 percent lower than a year ago, the state labor department said Tuesday.</p>
<p>The state's labor force remained virtually unchanged in April compared to one year ago, dropping 200 to 388,700, while the number of employed rose 2,000 to 378,200, the department said.</p>
<p>The U.S. unemployment rate for April was 4.9 percent, down from 5.2 percent in March.</p>
<p>((--David Bailey, 312-408-8647))</p>
